Description: mark the description as rebuilt
 Changes the busybox package's own description, which lives in
 debian/control. A patch that only touches debian/ is applied to the
 tree and ends up in the new debian tarball. This is here to make the
 example verifiable, not because the change is useful in itself.
Author: seine
Forwarded: not-needed

--- a/debian/control
+++ b/debian/control
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
 Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
 Conflicts: busybox-static
 Replaces: busybox-static
-Description: Tiny utilities for small and embedded systems
+Description: Tiny utilities for small and embedded systems (rebuilt-by-seine)
  BusyBox combines tiny versions of many common UNIX utilities into a single
  small executable. It provides minimalist replacements for the most common
  utilities you would usually find on your desktop system (i.e., ls, cp, mv,
